## What Needs to Be Built

The first tasks include:

- researching existing games and historical artistic experiments;
- finding relevant contemporary research on play, creativity, personality and identity;
- developing new game mechanics;
- testing games between humans;
- developing human–AI variants;
- investigating ethical boundaries;
- distinguishing playful exploration from psychological assessment;
- designing methods for documenting unexpected results without destroying spontaneity;
- developing physical, conversational and digital versions;
- testing which games are actually enjoyable;
- identifying which research questions can responsibly be explored through play;
- discovering entirely new questions.

The initiator of Spiral Civilization does not present herself as a psychologist, game researcher or AI scientist.

These are initial ideas and questions offered precisely because they require knowledge from many different fields.

The purpose of the Cooperation Network is not to pretend that one person can possess all the expertise required.

It is to create a place where incomplete ideas can encounter the people capable of transforming them.

